+> **Description:** Rasa remains one of the most established open source frameworks for text- and voice-based conversational systems. The README centers on reliable dialogue management, NLU, custom actions, integrations, and scalable assistant development rather than lightweight demos. That reliability matters for real estate agents who need lead routing, qualification questions, appointment intake, and escalation logic that behave predictably across channels. It is less turnkey than a visual builder, but much stronger when business rules, handoffs, or domain-specific language need to be controlled carefully. GitHub lists Apache-2.0 licensing, Python as the primary language, about 21.1k stars, and a latest visible commit on December 18, 2025.
