+
+# Best AI Tools for Real Estate Agents in 2026
+
+[![Awesome](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/sindresorhus/awesome@main/media/badge.svg)](https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
+![Topics](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/GagnDeep/awesome-best-ai-tools-for-real-estate-agents-2026?style=social)
+
+> Best AI tools for real estate agents in 2026 are still scattered across chat, workflow, document, mapping, and media projects rather than one clean software category. This list curates public GitHub repositories that real estate agents, brokers, marketers, and ops teams can actually self-host or extend for lead capture, follow-up automation, document handling, market research, and listing content workflows.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- `Flowise`, `Langflow`, `LibreChat`, and `Rasa` are the strongest starting points for building real estate lead bots, AI assistants, and website chat flows.
+- `Activepieces`, `Node-RED`, `Chatwoot`, `Mautic`, and `Bytebot` cover the follow-up, inbox, campaign, and back-office automation side.
+- `Paperless-ngx`, `Docling`, `OCRmyPDF`, `Tesseract`, and `Apache Tika` are the practical stack for contracts, disclosures, inspection PDFs, and intake documents.
+- `MicroRealEstate`, `RealEstateCRM`, `OpenEstate-IO`, `streamlit-geospatial`, and `flathunter` are the most directly relevant repos for property operations and market workflows.
+- `ComfyUI`, `stable-diffusion-webui`, `imagor-studio`, `virtual-staging`, and `Ollama` are useful for listing media, staging experiments, and local model execution.
+
+## Why This List
+Open source matters for real estate agents because client data, contracts, disclosures, lead pipelines, and listing assets are too sensitive to trap inside closed SaaS stacks by default. The best AI tools for real estate agents in 2026 are mostly self-hosted building blocks: conversational AI, workflow engines, OCR pipelines, geospatial apps, and image systems that can be combined into practical agent workflows.
+
+This list is intentionally honest about the market. There are still very few mature GitHub projects built only for real estate AI, so the strongest repositories are often broader open source tools that fit real estate use cases well. Where a repository uses a non-standard or source-available license, the license field is written exactly as shown on GitHub so you can filter it out if your policy requires OSI-only licensing.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+### AI Assistants & Lead Capture
+
+#### [Flowise](https://github.com/FlowiseAI/Flowise)
+> **Description:** Flowise is a visual builder for AI agents, RAG pipelines, and multi-step chatbot workflows. Its README focuses on no-code and low-code flow design, self-hosting, Docker deployment, API exposure, and an extensible node ecosystem for LLMs, vector stores, and tools. For real estate teams, that makes it well suited to website lead bots, buyer qualification flows, FAQ assistants, and internal knowledge copilots connected to office docs or property data. GitHub shows this repo is licensed under Apache-2.0, uses TypeScript primarily, has about 51.5k stars, and had its latest visible commit on April 2, 2026.
