+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for real estate agents in 2026?
+For most teams, the best starting stack is `Flowise` or `Langflow` for workflows, `LibreChat` for a private assistant UI, `Activepieces` or `Node-RED` for operational automation, and `Paperless-ngx` plus `OCRmyPDF` for documents. If you need a real-estate-native codebase, start by reviewing `RealEstateCRM`, `MicroRealEstate`, and `OpenEstate-IO`.
+
+### Are there many GitHub projects built only for real estate AI agents?
+No. That is the biggest gap this research surfaced. There are a handful of real-estate-specific repositories, but most strong options are broader open source AI, OCR, mapping, or automation tools that fit real estate workflows after configuration.
+
+### Which self-hosted AI chatbot is best for real estate lead capture?
+`Flowise`, `Langflow`, and `Rasa` are the strongest options depending on your team. Use `Flowise` for faster visual builds, `Langflow` for visual flows with deeper developer control, and `Rasa` when conversation rules, handoffs, and reliability matter more than speed.
+
+### What is the best open source document AI stack for real estate contracts and disclosures?
+`OCRmyPDF` plus `Tesseract` handle OCR, `Paperless-ngx` handles searchable storage, and `Docling` or `Apache Tika` handle deeper parsing and normalization. That combination is better than looking for one “magic” real estate contract AI repo.
+
+### Which GitHub tools help with real estate listing images and virtual staging?
+`ComfyUI`, `stable-diffusion-webui`, `imagor-studio`, and `virtual-staging` are the most relevant repos in this list. `imagor-studio` is best for practical image operations, while `ComfyUI` and `virtual-staging` are better for more technical generation and staging experiments.
+
+### Can I build a private local AI stack for a brokerage without a SaaS dependency?
+Yes. A realistic stack is `Ollama` for local model serving, `LibreChat` for the user interface, `Flowise` or `Langflow` for workflow logic, `Paperless-ngx` for document storage, and `Activepieces` or `Node-RED` for automation. That gives you much more control over data than defaulting to cloud-only tools.
+
+### Which categories are still weak in open source real estate AI?
+Purpose-built sales CRM AI, brokerage transaction management AI, and polished virtual staging products are still weak categories on GitHub. When a category has good repos today, it usually comes from general open source AI infrastructure rather than real-estate-native applications.
